WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.152
Before adding a language model, test whether retrieval works.

00:00:04.152 --> 00:00:10.287
We ask a question about internship registration and inspect the top three results.

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:17.117
The expected behavior is that the Internship Registration Checklist appears at or near the top.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:20.857
If it does not, stop here and investigate.

00:00:20.857 --> 00:00:24.127
This is a crucial RAG debugging principle.

00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:29.061
The language model cannot reliably answer from evidence that was never retrieved.

00:00:29.602 --> 00:00:36.330
When the wrong source is returned, look at the document text, chunking, embedding model, filters,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.995
and similarity method before changing the prompt.

00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:45.335
A lot of RAG development is really retrieval engineering.

00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:48.585
The model is only one layer in the system.

00:00:48.585 --> 00:00:53.215
So at this stage, treat the retrieved rows as the product.

00:00:53.215 --> 00:00:59.924
Read them carefully and ask whether you would be comfortable giving those passages to a model as evidence.
